    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499-a1">

                <pb facs="0869" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg799"/>

                <head>Mr. Wilson to Mr. Seijas</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of The United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Caracas,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 5, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The undersigned, minister resident of the
                    United States, has the honor to ask of your excellency what steps have been
                    taken by the government of Venezuela for the arrest and trial of Generals Sosa,
                    Juan Santos Mendez, and others, implicated in the murder of Captain <pb
                        facs="0870" n="800" xml:id="pg800"/> John W. Hammer, Julius de Brissot, and
                    the wounding of Joseph Stackpole, citizens of the United States, at Apurito, in
                    October last. Also, what provision, if any, has been made to indemnify the
                    widows and children or representatives of the sufferers.</p>
                <p>The undersigned renews to Mr. Seijas the assurance of his distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES WILSON.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rafael Seijas, Minister of Foreign
                            Relations, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
